# Command cards

When sharing terminal or git commands with the user:

- Put **one command per card** — each command in its own fenced code block.
- Do not split one command across multiple blocks.
- Do not put multiple separate commands in the same block (no `&&` chains unless it is a single intentional pipeline the user asked for).
- If several commands are needed, list them as separate cards in order.

Example:

```bash
git add js/standings.js
```

```bash
git commit -m "fix(wc26): keep Pts visible on mobile standings"
```

```bash
git push origin main
```

When running Shell tool calls, prefer one command per invocation when the user will see or copy the commands; batch only independent read-only checks (e.g. `git status`, `git diff`) when efficiency matters and the user did not ask for copy-paste steps.
